# Documentation Rules

Require professional code documentation.

## Requirements
- Exported functions, modules, classes, and complex logic must have JSDoc-style comments.
- Route handlers must document purpose, authentication, permissions, params, body, responses, and important side effects.
- Repositories and services must document scope assumptions, audit expectations, and non-obvious workflow constraints.
- Inline comments must explain intent or edge cases only.
- Code, migrations, seeds, and docs must be updated in the same change when behavior changes.
